# Vapi Studio project starter

This repo is a **consumer NestJS app** for `@guidify-ai/vapi-studio` — not the framework.

## Before changing conversation code

1. Read `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/docs/best-practices/README.md`
2. Read `node_modules/@guidify-ai/vapi-studio/agent/AGENTS.md`
3. Follow `.cursor/rules/vapi-studio-best-practices.mdc` and `ui-and-api-identity.mdc`

## Where to put work

| Change | Location |
| --- | --- |
| New agent step | `src/conversation/nodes/*.node.ts` + register in `app.module.ts` + `config/flow.yaml` |
| Routing / intentions | `config/flow.yaml` (+ optional intention helpers under `src/conversation/`) |
| Vapi webhook / Custom LLM | `src/vapi/` |
| Brain adapter | `src/brain/brain.config.ts` |
| Secrets | `.env` only (never commit) |
| Private overlays | `src/shadows/` (see README there) |

## Hard product rules (summary)

- One CTA per turn; conversations must end (`limits` always on)
- Fail-closed constrained extracts; short digit listen timeouts
- Soft affirmatives on multi-choice → local re-ask (not Brain/unknown)
- Silent handoffs; mad: one re-engage then transfer
- Async prep/teardown in `before()` / `after()` — do not overload `run()`
- External APIs: **uuid** only; DTOs include human **label**

## Do not

- Put application bots inside the `vapi-studio` framework package
- Speak raw `userText` / off-topic LLM output / node or graph names
- Rotate `config/project.identity.json` `id` after Vapi is wired
